<title>LEBANON: SHORTER-TERM T-BILL YIELDS FALL IN BEIRUT.</title>
<headline>SHORTER-TERM T-BILL YIELDS FALL IN BEIRUT.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields on three and six month Lebanese treasury bills for the August 14 issue continued falling while 12 and 24 month t-bill yields held steady, the Bank of Lebanon said on Monday.</p>
<p>The bank issued the following rate details (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				 percent)		    (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	   12.68 (12.70)		13.09 (13.12)</p>
<p>    Six months	     13.06 (13.08)		13.97 (13.99)</p>
<p>    12 month		 13.20 (13.20)		15.20 (15.20)</p>
<p>    24 month   (interest payable twice early)     16.08 (16.08)</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (9611) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
